TWO DIFFERENT MESSIAHS

A clear proof that the first and second Messiah would be different persons is found in the hadith collection Sahih Bukhari & Muslim

Hazrat Mirza Ghulam Ahmad, The Promised Messiah and Mahdi عليه السلام said:

“Now let us turn to our Holy Master and Mentor—the Holy Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, the Seal and Certificate of all Prophets. In order to single out the second Messiah from the first, the Holy Prophet ﷺ did not merely announce that the former would be a Muslim by faith; that he would conduct himself in accordance with the Quranic Law; that he would pray and fast and carry out other Quranic injunctions like a Muslim; that he would be a born Muslim; that he wouldn’t bring any new Law; and that he would not claim to be an independent Prophet. In addition to all this, the Holy Prophet ﷺ also disclosed that there would be a marked difference between the physical features of the two Messiahs.

The Holy Prophet ﷺ saw the first Messiah on the night of the Mi‘raj. According to a tradition mentioned in Sahih Bukhari (Book 60 Prophets), page 489 (Darus Salam, Riyad, 1997), the Holy Prophet ﷺ described him as of medium height, reddish complexion, curly hair, and a broad chest. But, in the same book, the Holy Prophet ﷺ is reported to have described the second Messiah as being of light brown complexion the colour of wheat, and having, not curly, but straight hair reaching down to his ears.

Let us pause for a moment and consider. Surely the distinguishing marks of the two Messiahs, as stated by the Holy Prophet ﷺ, adequately assure us that the first and second Messiah are two entirely different persons. As for addressing each of them as ‘the son of Mary’, this is a metaphor which is as subtle as it is fine: it has been employed on account of the temperamental and spiritual affinity between the two Messiahs. Is it not true that because of such resemblance in disposition and character, two different persons, known for their piety, may well be addressed by the same name, just as two bad characters, who equally share evil, may be called counterparts? Muslims often name their children after the names of Prophets such as Ahmad, Musa, ‘Isa, Sulaiman, Dawud, and so on. They do so as an augury, hoping that, as a good omen, the children thus named might acquire the spiritual qualities and character of these archetypal ideals to the extent of becoming their true copies.”

[Elucidation of Objectives, Pages 14-15]

The Promised Messiah and Mahdi عليه السلام is referring to the Messiah of the Children of Israel being described as having أَحْمَرُ (red) complexion with جَعْدٌ (curly hair), while the Messiah of the Latter Days has آدَمُ (brown) complexion with long سَبْطٌ (straight) hair. In this article we will analyse the two different descriptions from the ahadith.

MESSIAH TO THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL

First Meeting

The Holy Prophet ﷺ saw the first Messiah on the night of the Mi‘raj.

Anas ibn Malik reported:

“When Jibril and the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by Idris, the latter said, ‘Welcome, O pious Prophet and pious brother!’ the Prophet (ﷺ) asked, ‘Who is he?’ Jibril said, ‘He is Idris.’ ” The Prophet (ﷺ) added, “Then I passed by Musa who said, ‘Welcome, O pious Prophet and pious brother!’ I said, ‘Who is he?’ Jibril said, ‘He is Musa.’ Then I passed by ‘Isa who said, ‘Welcome, O pious Prophet and pious brother!’ I said, ‘Who is he?’ He replied, ‘He is ‘Isa.’ Then I passed by the Prophet (ﷺ) Ibrahim who said, ‘Welcome, O pious Prophet and pious son!’ I said, ‘Who is he?’ Jibril replied, ‘He is Ibrahim’.”

[Sahih al-Bukhari 3342, Book 60 Prophets]
{Also found in Sahih Muslim 163, Book 1 The Book of Faith & Musnad Ahmad 21185}

Physical Description

According to a tradition mentioned in Sahih Bukhari (Book 60 Prophets), the Holy Prophet ﷺ described him as of medium height, reddish (أَحْمَرُ) complexion, curly hair (جَعْدٌ), and a broad chest.

Narrated Abu Huraira:

The Prophet (ﷺ) said, “I met Moses on the night of my Ascension to heaven.” The Prophet (ﷺ) then described him saying, as I think, “He was a tall person with (سَبْطٌ) lank hair as if he belonged to the people of the tribe of Shanu’s.’ The Prophet (ﷺ) further said, “I met Jesus.” The Prophet (ﷺ) described him saying, “He was one of moderate height and was red-faced as if he had just come out of a bathroom. I saw Abraham whom I resembled more than any of his children did.” The Prophet (ﷺ) further said, “(That night) I was given two cups; one full of milk and the other full of wine. I was asked to take either of them which I liked, and I took the milk and drank it. On that it was said to me, ‘You have taken the right path (religion). If you had taken the wine, your (Muslim) nation would have gone astray.”

[Sahih al-Bukhari 3437, Book 60 Prophets]
{Shanua are a tribe from Yemen, who have a brown complexion}

Narrated Ibn `Abbas:

The Prophet (ﷺ) said, “I saw Moses, Jesus and Abraham (on the night of my Ascension to the heavens). Jesus was of (حْمَرُ) red complexion, (جَعْدٌ) curly hair and a broad chest. Moses was of (آدَمُ) brown complexion, (سَبْطٌ) straight hair and tall stature as if he was from the people of Az-Zutt.”

[Sahih al-Bukhari 3438, Book 60 Prophets]
{Az-Zutt are Jats from the Indian Subcontinent, who have a wheatish complexion}

MESSIAH TO THE MUSLIM UMMAH

First Meeting & Physical Description

But, in the same book, the Holy Prophet ﷺ is reported to have described the second Messiah as being of light (آدَمُ) brown complexion the colour of wheat, and having, not (جَعْدٌ) curly, but (آدَمُ) straight hair reaching down to his ears.

Narrated `Abdullah Ibn Umar:

The Prophet (ﷺ) mentioned the Masih Ad-Dajjal in front of the people saying, Allah is not one-eyed while Masih Ad-Dajjal is blind in the right eye and his eye looks like a bulging out grape. While sleeping near the Ka`ba last night, I saw in my dream a man of (آدَمُ) brown colour the best one can see amongst (أُدْمِ) brown colour, and his hair was long that it fell between his shoulders. His hair was (سَبْطٌ) lank and water was dribbling from his head, and he was placing his hands on the shoulders of two men while circumambulating the Ka`ba. I asked, ‘Who is this?’ They replied, ‘This is Jesus, son of Mary.’ Behind him I saw a man who had very (جَعْدٌ) curly hair and was blind in the right eye, resembling Ibn Qatan (i.e. an infidel) in appearance. He was placing his hands on the shoulders of a person while performing Tawaf around the Ka`ba. I asked, ‘Who is this? ‘They replied, ‘The Masih, Ad-Dajjal.’ “

[Sahih al-Bukhari 3439, 3440, Book 60 Prophets]

Narrated Salim from his father (`Abdullah Ibn Umar):

No, By Allah, the Prophet (ﷺ) did not tell that Jesus was of (حْمَرُ) red complexion but said, “While I was asleep circumambulating the Ka`ba (in my dream), suddenly I saw a man of (آدَمُ) brown complexion and (سَبْطٌ) lank hair walking between two men, and water was dropping from his head. I asked, ‘Who is this?’ The people said, ‘He is the son of Mary.’ Then I looked behind and I saw a (حْمَرُ) red-complexioned, fat, (جَعْدٌ) curly-haired man, blind in the right eye which looked like a bulging out grape. I asked, ‘Who is this?’ They replied, ‘He is Ad-Dajjal.’ The one who resembled to him among the people, was Ibn Qatar.” (Az-Zuhri said, “He (Ibn Qatan) was a man from the tribe Khuza`a who died in the pre-lslamic period.”

[Sahih al-Bukhari 3441, Book 60 Prophets]

DIFFERENT VARIATIONS

Below are all the hadith from Bukhari & Muslim on the physical appearance of the Messiahs عليهم السلام, both Imam Bukhari & Imam Muslim organised these 2 different descriptions in their sahih in such a way as to show contrast, discerptions placed earlier in their collections all being of the Mosaic Messiah while the latter for the Messiah to come even within the same chapter:

Imam Bukhari:

1st Messiah:
*Sahih al-Bukhari 3239, Book 59 Beginning of Creation
Sahih al-Bukhari 3394, Book 60 Prophets
Sahih al-Bukhari 3395, 3396, Book 60 Prophets
Sahih al-Bukhari 3437, Book 60 Prophets
Sahih al-Bukhari 3438, Book 60 Prophets
